{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities","id":813864,"title":"Mystery of Humanities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-21T20:09:42-08:00","id":813864,"title":"Mystery of Humanities","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Was kicking around some ideas for an Ordo of Dracul Mystery that revolved around Humanity and the long term conflict between the Man and Beast within Vampires, and below are the Coils of Humanities that I have come up with. I have not yet had time to give the Mystery of Humanities a full write up with sample Scales, but I am presenting what I have so you folks may kick the tires and give me some feed back. I am as interested in Mechanical Opinions as I am Opinions about the Flavor Text.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Coils of the Humanities</b></u></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sisyphean Fortitude\u2022</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is an ever present current of want, eroding away what Humanity remains until nothing remains but want. Those who have mastered this coil have learned to better endure the storm that is the every present threat of the Beast upon their Sanity. Whenever the Dragon rolls for Detachment add their Coils of Humanities Rank to their Detachment Dice Pool to maintain Humanity. In addition to this an Exceptional Success can be achieved with 3 Successes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Koinonein \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To Divide and Conquer is a time tested and proven tactic, and the Beast knows it well. One of the more subtle and ruthless attacks upon the Mind of the Man is the Beast's efforts to isolate the Man from others. By making the Man feel removed from Humanity, he is removed from the herd and easier prey for the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil have learned how to keep their place in the Herd despite the Beast's best efforts. Add the Dragon's ranks in the Coils of Humanities in regards to interacting with Humanity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Promethus in the Cave of Hypnos\u2022 \u2022 \u2022</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The forced Hibernation of Topor is another of the Beasts threats to the Mind of Man. Through removing the Man from Humanity for vast cycles of time it forces the Man to see himself as an entity separate from the present, separate from the People of Today, always a creature of the past and of the future. In making the Man unfocused upon the present and uncaring for those who live within it, the Beast makes it easier for the Man to give in to the ever present Temptations of the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil have learned to steel themselves against the Beast's Call to Hibernate as an Animal. Dragons add their ranks in the Coil of Humanities to their Humanity for purposes of determining the length of their Topor.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Man Beneath Morpheus \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is never truly at rest. Even within the deep hibernation of Topor, or the slumber of Day Sleep the Beast is Hungry for more, it's mind races with the revelry of past and future hunts, always denying the mind of Man the Rest it needs to fully recover. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanity are no longer the victims of the Beast's hunger when they close their eyes. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanities may regain 1 point of Willpower from Day Sleep the same as Mortals regain Willpower from a Night's Rest.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Human Under Helios \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is a Nocturnal Predator, Man is not. The Light of Day does not Burn Man, it Burns the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered the Fifth and Final Coil of Humanities stand dominate over the Beast, while it cowers in the shadow of Man. Because the Dragon's Beast cowers within the shadow of Man, the Dragon is afforded some protection from the light of day. The Dragon may as Instant action spend Willpower to to increase their Humanity Rating for One Scene. This use of Willpower does count as their use of Willpower for the Round, but for purposes of this Coil the Dragon can spend as many Willpower Points as they desire to increase their effective Humanity Rating for the Scene. The Dragon's modified Humanity for the Scene is the Humanity that is used to determine the penalty or Damage they receive for any and all Banes that use Humanity as part of their formula. This includes the Damage Dealt by Sun Light.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","user":"JMecha","date":". 01-21-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T21:27:41-08:00","id":813899,"title":"","content":"Huh. This is a really interesting Mystery of the Dragon. Aside from answering my question on whether or not Kindred gain Willpower, by default, these benefits are fitting for its theme. Looking forward to your write-ups for its Scales (and, on that note, I should probably be revisiting my Mystery of Slumber to get some decent Scales done).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T01:08:28-08:00","id":813975,"title":"","content":"Two glaring problems I see with this coil:<br /> First, well, not much of a problem, but, this seems like this should by a banned coil by the ordo, because at start it feels like just defending and being more like human... when the main stray of ordo says to become better than a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, the first three dots are all passive, which do not enable you to do anything new, take a look at the other coils all of them with each dot give the character something new to do, somehow else to interact with the story and launch it forward... here, the first three will not enable any new stories to be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T09:41:52-08:00","id":814191,"title":"","content":"I am going to start with a little disclaimer. I dont claim to know everything and at times I am wrong. With that said.<br /> <br /> I also struggled with finding out if Vampires get the willpower point back for daysleep. No where does it say you don't, so I have always played with it as you do and the mask/dirge is just like the vice/virtue, an additional help to get it back. <br /> <br /> I am going to agree with Griatuis. I think this totally goes against what the Ordo is all about. It is about becoming a better vampire, not becoming ( or staying ) human. so This doesnt quite fit their theme. May I ask why you want it to be Ordo in the first place? Perhaps a unique bloodline discipline instead? <br /> <br /> Just picky now: Torpor <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T09:54:38-08:00","id":814202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=814191#post814191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also struggled with finding out if Vampires get the willpower point back for daysleep. No where does it say you don't, so I have always played with it as you do and the mask/dirge is just like the vice/virtue, an additional help to get it back.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This has been clarified by the developers several times already... Once just today in a different thread. Book does not say they do, which means they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:04:49-08:00","id":814213,"title":"","content":"I would agree with the thematic concerns raised above. Maybe switch the mentality away from &quot;How do I stop from becoming less human&quot; to &quot;How do I turn becoming less human into an advantage I can use?&quot;<br /> <br /> More like - would it be possible to turn that downward spiral of humanity into momentum you can use for other benefits? Ex: Whenever you fail a detachment check, add a bonus to all Ride the Wave (or experimentation, or Social Maneuver) attempts for the rest of the scene/session. Or, when facing a detachment check, you may allow yourself to fall into an immediate uncontrolled frenzy to gain a bonus on the check. Allow a willing, uncontrolled frenzy to act as a meaningful interaction with your Touchstone. Lots of ways you could go.<br /> <br /> Regardless of theme, I think the first dot might be too powerful, especially if you've mastered the Mystery. +4 or +5 dice to every detachment check basically means you have good odds of passing every sin except diablerie and the embrace. I would worry that makes it trivial to ignore a big conflict inherent in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:13:01-08:00","id":814219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=814202#post814202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has been clarified by the developers several times already... Once just today in a different thread. Book does not say they do, which means they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't read all the threads and that's my bad! Thanks! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:20:24-08:00","id":814226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=814213#post814213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree with the thematic concerns raised above. Maybe switch the mentality away from &quot;How do I stop from becoming less human&quot; to &quot;How do I turn becoming less human into an advantage I can use?&quot;<br /> <br /> More like - would it be possible to turn that downward spiral of humanity into momentum you can use for other benefits? Ex: Whenever you fail a detachment check, add a bonus to all Ride the Wave (or experimentation, or Social Maneuver) attempts for the rest of the scene/session. Or, when facing a detachment check, you may allow yourself to fall into an immediate uncontrolled frenzy to gain a bonus on the check. Allow a willing, uncontrolled frenzy to act as a meaningful interaction with your Touchstone. Lots of ways you could go.<br /> <br /> Regardless of theme, I think the first dot might be too powerful, especially if you've mastered the Mystery. +4 or +5 dice to every detachment check basically means you have good odds of passing every sin except diablerie and the embrace. I would worry that makes it trivial to ignore a big conflict inherent in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh those things you suggest sound exactly spot on what a Coil of such themes could do. Enable you to do something new in regards to humanity. This is not what it does in it's current itteration, hence the concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:36:29-08:00","id":814241,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong with applying the lessons of the Dragon in a heretical way. Wouldn't be the first or the last time such a thing happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:27:58-08:00","id":814379,"title":"","content":"Yes, but then it's heretical and that should be noted. <br /> <br /> It's still against coil guidelines of them allowing you to do stuff, instead of stopping it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T14:11:41-08:00","id":814447,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I follow the distinction you want to make there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T20:23:18-08:00","id":814626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=813975#post813975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two glaring problems I see with this coil:<br /> First, well, not much of a problem, but, this seems like this should by a banned coil by the ordo, because at start it feels like just defending and being more like human... when the main stray of ordo says to become better than a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, the first three dots are all passive, which do not enable you to do anything new, take a look at the other coils all of them with each dot give the character something new to do, somehow else to interact with the story and launch it forward... here, the first three will not enable any new stories to be told.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have not yet had time to bang out the full write up for the ideals behind the Mystery of Humanities, but I would ask you do not think of it as the &quot;Be more Human Coil&quot;. Try and frame it in your mind as the Coil that helps the Vampire endure the ever present efforts of the Beast to erode away all that it needs to create a Draugr. The original inspiration for the coil was a Character who's Requiem consisted of his best efforts to not let the Beast consume him. The idea is not for the Vampire to be more Human, the idea is for the Dragon to maintain their sense of self despite the Beast's best efforts to see that shredded and ravaged until only the Beast remains. The Dragon's efforts in developing means to thwart the Beast's efforts and preserve their Man Mind, or Rational Mind, or Sense of Self, The Bonuses to Humanity are not to represent the Vampire being more Human, but more so the Vampire's Beast having a little less sway over the Vampire's Requiem.<br /> <br /> The Beast is Hunger, the Beast is Rage, the Beast is Fear, etc....<br /> The Beast though is ultimately a predator and whatever &quot;Man Mind&quot; that remains within the Vampire is the prey. This Mystery is to help prevent the Vampire from falling prey to some of the Beast's more subtle efforts to see the &quot;Man Mind&quot; eroded away. The name &quot;Mystery of Humanities&quot; was taken, as was some of the Greek theme because the character that inspired this was a Greek scholarly type so the names seemed to fit his theme. <br /> <br /> Mystery of Humanities = Mystery of all the things that separate you from being a cave dwelling animal<br /> <br /> Which kinda makes the Coils desirable for any Neonates who do not want to let their being a Vampire make them a Monster, and extremely useful for any Elders who do not want their being a Monster deny them what little remains of who they are. Some may even say that extremely Monstrous Elder Vampires would have the most to gain from this coil<br /> <br /> As for the First Three Dots being Passive..... <br /> <br /> With the Dragon getting a bonus to detachment checks, will the Dragon begin to believe they have Transcended the need for Touchstones and start burning useless bridges? Will The Dragon who regularly feels remorse for Sins decide to make an effort to climb the Humanity Scale and be less of a Monster? or Will the Bonus Dice to Detachment Checks inspire a bit of reckless carelessness in the Dragon who decides that no matter what they do the Beast can not have them.....what does the all night society do with a member like that?<br /> <br /> A Dragon who is no longer suffering a penalty for interacting with Mortals, or even possibly getting a bonus for such interactions....what doors and opportunities does that create? The wedge that worked to separate the Dragon from the Mortal Population of the World has been removed or at a minimal weakened....how will that change the character's outlook, behavior, and options?<br /> <br /> As for the Torpor One.....that one's Passiveness and or Usefulness really changes table to table. At some tables it will make the difference between a Character in Torpor through some really fun and exciting swaths of time, and at other tables the Interesting Bits will be rearranged so they take place after any unexpected or inconvenient Torpor.<br /> <br /> I do not feel the coils I presented are exceptionally Passive compared to the Three Mysterious in the Core Book, maybe you are seeing something I am not? or hell maybe I am seeing something in my write up because it is mine and I am bias as hell? Either way I will review them again and compare them to the other existing coils to see if there is anything I do to make them less passive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T20:33:47-08:00","id":814633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=814213#post814213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree with the thematic concerns raised above. Maybe switch the mentality away from &quot;How do I stop from becoming less human&quot; to &quot;How do I turn becoming less human into an advantage I can use?&quot;<br /> <br /> More like - would it be possible to turn that downward spiral of humanity into momentum you can use for other benefits? Ex: Whenever you fail a detachment check, add a bonus to all Ride the Wave (or experimentation, or Social Maneuver) attempts for the rest of the scene/session. Or, when facing a detachment check, you may allow yourself to fall into an immediate uncontrolled frenzy to gain a bonus on the check. Allow a willing, uncontrolled frenzy to act as a meaningful interaction with your Touchstone. Lots of ways you could go.<br /> <br /> Regardless of theme, I think the first dot might be too powerful, especially if you've mastered the Mystery. +4 or +5 dice to every detachment check basically means you have good odds of passing every sin except diablerie and the embrace. I would worry that makes it trivial to ignore a big conflict inherent in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The current Theme of the Mystery is &quot; How not to Let The Beast inevitably make you a cave dwelling animal.&quot; Now I like the idea of there being a Mystery that allows Dragons to find empowerment through sliding down the Humanity Scale and becoming more beastial, but this particular coil is not that.<br /> <br /> As for the First Dot being Over Powered.....I am open to suggestions to make it less Over Powered.<br /> <br /> One Idea I had was to Allow the Dragon to Roll their Coil Rating and treat those Dice as a Team Work Bonus, but the turn off for me there is the Detachment Check just went from One Roll of Dice to Two Separate Rolls. I rather not make things more complicated then needed, or take twice as long.<br /> <br /> Another Idea I had was to only make the Coil Rating Bonus to Detachment Rolls available if the Dragon spends a Point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> +1 Die early and +5 Dice after 20 experience points did not seem game breaking to me at first, but maybe it is......any suggestions for a more balanced mechanic are welcomed<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T04:24:50-08:00","id":814770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities#post813864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#000000][FONT=Calibri][SIZE=16px]Was kicking around some ideas for an Ordo of Dracul Mystery that revolved around Humanity and the long term conflict between the Man and Beast within Vampires, and below are the Coils of Humanities that I have come up with. I have not yet had time to give the Mystery of Humanities a full write up with sample Scales, but I am presenting what I have so you folks may kick the tires and give me some feed back. I am as interested in Mechanical Opinions as I am Opinions about the Flavor Text.</div> </div> </div> </div>These... seem almost repeating. Add dots to this. Add dots to that. Add dots over there. It feels like, with the exception of the first dot to resist degeneration, this is just effectively adding dots to your Humanity score. Now, here's where I run into something of an issue. It costs 3exp for affinity, 4xp for non. I can buy Humanity for 2xp each. That means that, for the cost of purchasing the second and third tier, I can buy 3 to 4 dots of Humanity. Not only am I getting more dots of Humanity for the same price, but those dots of Humanity are more generally applicable - against banes, relating to humans, for torpor.<br /> <br /> The fourth dot is implied in text, but it was excluded from the final book, so it should be notable that not everyone plays with that rule. As well, its usefullness depends on how generous the ST is with willpower restoration from other sources - Mask and Dirge effectively give you two Virtues / Vices above everyone else. If you get those with any regularity, then recovering willpower during the day is a bit redundant. If its scarce, its much more attractive.<br /> <br /> I don't like the fifth dot due to its overlap with the Mystery of the Ascendent, which has a similar power (Epidermal Shielding Bath).<br /> <br /> While I like the idea behind the Coil, everything but the very first and fourth dots are cheaper and more effective to purchase other Mysteries, Majesty/Auspex, or dots of Humanity. Regaining willpower and resisting degeneration are nice ideas, and I'm personally lackluster on the latter idea. Only the fourth dot really appeals to me in any way, and even that depends on STs. I don't see the appeal of the Coil when we could do similar for less XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-23-2016, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T04:41:00-08:00","id":814773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities#post813864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man Beneath Morpheus (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> The Beast is never truly at rest. Even within the deep hibernation of Topor, or the slumber of Day Sleep the Beast is Hungry for more, it's mind races with the revelry of past and future hunts, always denying the mind of Man the Rest it needs to fully recover. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanity are no longer the victims of the Beast's hunger when they close their eyes. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanities may regain 1 point of Willpower from Day Sleep the same as Mortals regain Willpower from a Night's Rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's alright, you mind if I take this Coil to form part of my conversion of the Coil of Slumber? I already have it posted on Pendragon's Requiem Homebrew Hub. But I was thinking of revisiting it again to see if I could improve it somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T04:46:04-08:00","id":814777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=814626#post814626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the First Three Dots being Passive.....<br /> <br /> With the Dragon getting a bonus to detachment checks, will the Dragon begin to believe they have Transcended the need for Touchstones and start burning useless bridges? Will The Dragon who regularly feels remorse for Sins decide to make an effort to climb the Humanity Scale and be less of a Monster? or Will the Bonus Dice to Detachment Checks inspire a bit of reckless carelessness in the Dragon who decides that no matter what they do the Beast can not have them.....what does the all night society do with a member like that?<br /> <br /> A Dragon who is no longer suffering a penalty for interacting with Mortals, or even possibly getting a bonus for such interactions....what doors and opportunities does that create? The wedge that worked to separate the Dragon from the Mortal Population of the World has been removed or at a minimal weakened....how will that change the character's outlook, behavior, and options?<br /> <br /> As for the Torpor One.....that one's Passiveness and or Usefulness really changes table to table. At some tables it will make the difference between a Character in Torpor through some really fun and exciting swaths of time, and at other tables the Interesting Bits will be rearranged so they take place after any unexpected or inconvenient Torpor.<br /> <br /> I do not feel the coils I presented are exceptionally Passive compared to the Three Mysterious in the Core Book, maybe you are seeing something I am not? or hell maybe I am seeing something in my write up because it is mine and I am bias as hell? Either way I will review them again and compare them to the other existing coils to see if there is anything I do to make them less passive.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, the are all passive. As in, it doesn't encourage people to go out and do things. Its all reactionary. <br /> <br /> Touchstones do more than resist detachment. It talks you down from frenzy as well. Someone with high willpower will eventually feel less need for a Touchstone, sure. Especially the Ventrue, but that's part of the game. Touchstones have a lot of thematic impact on the game, and merely adding a bonus to resist degeneration isn't going to negate that. You'll need more.<br /> <br /> I can not suffer a penalty for interacting with mortals with a simple application of Majesty 1 (for appearance issues) and Auspex 1 (for empathy check issues). What doors and opertunities it creates? That depends entirely on who's running the game. 9 times of 10, you won't be opening more doors than the Daeva will. And it still depends on you reacting to the stimuli the ST provides.<br /> <br /> The Coils are passive because they all depend on the ST doing things, and then coming up in niche cases. Coil of the Wyrm? All about Riding the Wave. Frenzy threatens? You ride it, do something bad ass you choose to do, then snap out of it. A Nightmare/Majesty user threatened with a Pred Aura? Snap into frenzy, Aura back with larger dice pool, shrug off back to normal. Battle? You Ride again. Coil of the Voivode - go out and blood bond, get massive blood sympathy bonuses, create a dynasty from your blood. Coil of the Ascendant? Go out and play in the sun. Each Coil pushes you to do -more-. You don't learn Coils to sit there and shrug off bad things. You learn Coils to gain power and advantage over your rivals and enemies. <br /> <br /> Each of the core book Coils are deliberately provoking you to do -something-. To go out and make stories. Simply resisting detachment is not very story fulfilling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:39:57-08:00","id":815042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=814773#post814773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's alright, you mind if I take this Coil to form part of my conversion of the Coil of Slumber? I already have it posted on Pendragon's Requiem Homebrew Hub. But I was thinking of revisiting it again to see if I could improve it somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please by all means take the Coils I presented and use and abuse them however you like. Pick and Pull what you want and have at it. The whole reason I posted the Coils of Humanities was to get feed back from the community and share what I am working on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:46:14-08:00","id":815048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=814777#post814777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, the are all passive. As in, it doesn't encourage people to go out and do things. Its all reactionary. <br /> <br /> Touchstones do more than resist detachment. It talks you down from frenzy as well. Someone with high willpower will eventually feel less need for a Touchstone, sure. Especially the Ventrue, but that's part of the game. Touchstones have a lot of thematic impact on the game, and merely adding a bonus to resist degeneration isn't going to negate that. You'll need more.<br /> <br /> I can not suffer a penalty for interacting with mortals with a simple application of Majesty 1 (for appearance issues) and Auspex 1 (for empathy check issues). What doors and opertunities it creates? That depends entirely on who's running the game. 9 times of 10, you won't be opening more doors than the Daeva will. And it still depends on you reacting to the stimuli the ST provides.<br /> <br /> The Coils are passive because they all depend on the ST doing things, and then coming up in niche cases. Coil of the Wyrm? All about Riding the Wave. Frenzy threatens? You ride it, do something bad ass you choose to do, then snap out of it. A Nightmare/Majesty user threatened with a Pred Aura? Snap into frenzy, Aura back with larger dice pool, shrug off back to normal. Battle? You Ride again. Coil of the Voivode - go out and blood bond, get massive blood sympathy bonuses, create a dynasty from your blood. Coil of the Ascendant? Go out and play in the sun. Each Coil pushes you to do -more-. You don't learn Coils to sit there and shrug off bad things. You learn Coils to gain power and advantage over your rivals and enemies. <br /> <br /> Each of the core book Coils are deliberately provoking you to do -something-. To go out and make stories. Simply resisting detachment is not very story fulfilling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am picking up what you are putting down and you have my thanks for the feed back. If you have any suggestions as to how the Humanities Coils could be reworked to be less passive I would be very excited to see your examples","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T05:18:40-08:00","id":815368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=815048#post815048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am picking up what you are putting down and you have my thanks for the feed back. If you have any suggestions as to how the Humanities Coils could be reworked to be less passive I would be very excited to see your examples</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, one thing I would suggest is thinking about the Annoshka's Ladder. Its both a secret society within the Ordo, and a Coil from 1e. Its basically reaching for Golconda, and the Sworn were the nWoD equivalent to the oWoD Inconnu. Playing up the Sworn of the Ladder is one thing you could do. Shedding vampire abilities to gain advantages could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Another I suggest is taking a look at Secret of the Covenant Ordo Preview. There's a Coil of Ziva that can be mined for ideas. Its probably going to be heavily revamped (no pun intended), but I do like the idea of &quot;diablarizing humanity&quot; from other vampires or people. You steal bits of their soul to graft onto yours. <br /> <br /> Or maybe psychically passing on the traits to others? Go Sin-Eater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-24-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:52:17-08:00","id":815931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=815042#post815042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please by all means take the Coils I presented and use and abuse them however you like. Pick and Pull what you want and have at it. The whole reason I posted the Coils of Humanities was to get feed back from the community and share what I am working on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> And here's my take on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=726633#post726633\">Mystery of Slumber</a>, if you're curious. I'm still figuring out what Scales could be derived from the Coil, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:52:58-08:00","id":821421,"title":"","content":"I actually liked the flavor of the Coil, and can easily see it as mainstream in the Ordo, not as a heretical Coil.<br /> <br /> Yes, Humanity is a weakness for a vampire. But what the Coil do to protect it serves for the vampire to <u>ignore</u> the weakness.<br /> <br /> That in mind, I think the first dot is good enough. It is strong, but not overpowered in my opinion. Yes, it does hurt a central theme of the game, but this is what every Coil do! They are about going against vampire weaknesses (even Coil of the Wyrm grants more control of frenzy as you start to take it into account instead of avoiding it). It can simply be banned for players when the chronicle demands, as should be any other Coil, but doesn't seem specially bad as default.<br /> <br /> But the complains about passiveness are very valid. I loved the flavor, but the rules are too much reactive, and mostly positively weak. Let me revise each one, it is easier for me:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sisyphean Fortitude\u2022</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is an ever present current of want, eroding away what Humanity remains until nothing remains but want. Those who have mastered this coil have learned to better endure the storm that is the every present threat of the Beast upon their Sanity. Whenever the Dragon rolls for Detachment add their Coils of Humanities Rank to their Detachment Dice Pool to maintain Humanity. In addition to this an Exceptional Success can be achieved with 3 Successes.</span></span></span></span><br /> This seems good enough. If much, it could be turned to another level. It makes possible for the vampire to keep its sanity while being completely atrocious. Another possibility could be to let the vampire develop a Ban to prevent a specific Breaking Point <b><u>before</u></b> doing the act, but maybe it is better reserved for a scale. A possibility for putting a little limit on the use of the bonus could be to link it to the Meditation roll.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Koinonein \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To Divide and Conquer is a time tested and proven tactic, and the Beast knows it well. One of the more subtle and ruthless attacks upon the Mind of the Man is the Beast's efforts to isolate the Man from others. By making the Man feel removed from Humanity, he is removed from the herd and easier prey for the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil have learned how to keep their place in the Herd despite the Beast's best efforts. Add the Dragon's ranks in the Coils of Humanities in regards to interacting with Humanity.</span></span></span></span><br /> This one seems a little off even in the flavor, but starts too good to be ignored. Maybe at this stage, the Dragon could start to develop personas to deal with humans, assuming full effect of the idea of Humanity as the ability to mimic the Herd. Thinking quickly about Protean <b>Predatory Aspect</b>, I think similar bonuses could be developed for human interactions as &quot;personality aspects&quot;. It would be more interesting, less passive, synergistic with Majesty instead of overlapping, and at the same time more inhuman even being Human.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Promethus in the Cave of Hypnos\u2022 \u2022 \u2022</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The forced Hibernation of Topor is another of the Beasts threats to the Mind of Man. Through removing the Man from Humanity for vast cycles of time it forces the Man to see himself as an entity separate from the present, separate from the People of Today, always a creature of the past and of the future. In making the Man unfocused upon the present and uncaring for those who live within it, the Beast makes it easier for the Man to give in to the ever present Temptations of the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil have learned to steel themselves against the Beast's Call to Hibernate as an Animal. Dragons add their ranks in the Coil of Humanities to their Humanity for purposes of determining the length of their Topor.</span></span></span></span><br /> This needs a lot of work. Torpor is something that isolates the vampire, but also something that prepares it for the new times, specially when the Fog of Eternity enters play. But it reduces actual power. And what's worse, it rarely enters play truly. For most games (I know there are a lot of exceptions), a long torpor is as good as death for practical game purposes. And simply reducing its length don't make it more interesting. A Coil that works Torpor should make Torpor something that will enter play a lot, as the Coil of the Wyrm makes with Frenzy (from avoiding at all cost, the PC starts to want it). Maybe this Coil could let the vampire go into Torpor for controlled lengths of time (in a span that is actually playable, weeks at the <u>worst</u>), to reap true benefits from it. As a first draft, I would let each day of Torpor eliminate 1XP in Abilities or other traits approved by the ST, as the character forgets to make room for the new, and this induced freshness of the mind lets it relocate the XP removed to new Abilities at the same rate. It doesn't seem really good to me as written, but something in this direction, I don't have the time to work it better now.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Man Beneath Morpheus \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is never truly at rest. Even within the deep hibernation of Topor, or the slumber of Day Sleep the Beast is Hungry for more, it's mind races with the revelry of past and future hunts, always denying the mind of Man the Rest it needs to fully recover. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanity are no longer the victims of the Beast's hunger when they close their eyes. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanities may regain 1 point of Willpower from Day Sleep the same as Mortals regain Willpower from a Night's Rest.</span></span></span></span><br /> This is just too weak a benefit even for first level. For fourth it is laughable. But what about bringing Man and Beast to the same level? Or even inverting them? One benefit I think is of the reversing relation of Man and Beast during Daysleep: the vampire actualy let its Beast take control during Day, its most weak of times, while the Man rests, but is still wake enough to get the leash. The vampire enters a state of constant frenzy by day, but the Man can intercede at any moment to force down the Beast spending 1 WP. Being day, it is mostly a self-preserving tactic, with the Beast being able to defend itself with all its superlative strength, but barred everywhere by its own coward nature (because as any savage animal, the Beast is truly a coward facing any real danger. Throw in some more benefits, like bonuses for resisting frenzies during the night when your Beast had all day active, and that is my current idea. This is a tough one.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Human Under Helios \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is a Nocturnal Predator, Man is not. The Light of Day does not Burn Man, it Burns the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered the Fifth and Final Coil of Humanities stand dominate over the Beast, while it cowers in the shadow of Man. Because the Dragon's Beast cowers within the shadow of Man, the Dragon is afforded some protection from the light of day. The Dragon may as Instant action spend Willpower to to increase their Humanity Rating for One Scene. This use of Willpower does count as their use of Willpower for the Round, but for purposes of this Coil the Dragon can spend as many Willpower Points as they desire to increase their effective Humanity Rating for the Scene. The Dragon's modified Humanity for the Scene is the Humanity that is used to determine the penalty or Damage they receive for any and all Banes that use Humanity as part of their formula. This includes the Damage Dealt by Sun Light.</span></span></span></span><br /> This here really is too similar to another Coil, but not beyond hope. The core idea is to keep your Mind under the sun, not the body necessarily. To use the sun against the Beast. I'm thinking about something to get advantages against Degeneration and Frenzy from the sun, or from a sunburn. Or maybe an advantage to other mental tasks or powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:49:41-08:00","id":821728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=821421#post821421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Human Under Helios \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is a Nocturnal Predator, Man is not. The Light of Day does not Burn Man, it Burns the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered the Fifth and Final Coil of Humanities stand dominate over the Beast, while it cowers in the shadow of Man. Because the Dragon's Beast cowers within the shadow of Man, the Dragon is afforded some protection from the light of day. The Dragon may as Instant action spend Willpower to to increase their Humanity Rating for One Scene. This use of Willpower does count as their use of Willpower for the Round, but for purposes of this Coil the Dragon can spend as many Willpower Points as they desire to increase their effective Humanity Rating for the Scene. The Dragon's modified Humanity for the Scene is the Humanity that is used to determine the penalty or Damage they receive for any and all Banes that use Humanity as part of their formula. This includes the Damage Dealt by Sun Light.</span></span></span></span><br /> This here really is too similar to another Coil, but not beyond hope. The core idea is to keep your Mind under the sun, not the body necessarily. To use the sun against the Beast. I'm thinking about something to get advantages against Degeneration and Frenzy from the sun, or from a sunburn. Or maybe an advantage to other mental tasks or powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of the Overlap with the Mysteries of the Ascended, but I kind of like that the top tier coils of two different Mysteries attack the whole Sunlight Weakness from two different angles. Would allow a Dragon who has Mastered Both to potential endure Sunlight as well as a Blood Potency 1, Humanity 10 Vampire, even if they are far from such. With that being said RL has got me all tied up and I have not had the time to return to this project for further revising and editing, but I will in time...eventually. I just wanted to pop in and thank you for your suggestions and ideas, the feed back helps and I will make use of it moving forward....even if it will not likely be anytime this week or next.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T17:14:57-08:00","id":821989,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea, when it occurred me, of a master of the Coil burning itself on the sun as a way to gain ultimate control over the Beast. I'm struggling with ideas to put this on rules, but it seemed cool.<br /> <br /> And the best way to create sinergy between two powers isn't to make them add together, but effectively make them create distinct effects that work well together. Otherwise it seems just more of the same, something better off as a scale, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:10:36-08:00","id":822022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=821989#post821989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the idea, when it occurred me, of a master of the Coil burning itself on the sun as a way to gain ultimate control over the Beast. I'm struggling with ideas to put this on rules, but it seemed cool.<br /> <br /> And the best way to create sinergy between two powers isn't to make them add together, but effectively make them create distinct effects that work well together. Otherwise it seems just more of the same, something better off as a scale, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805100-bloodline-bak-ra#post805100\">Funny enough, I have a conversion of the Bak-Ra who <i>can</i> burn themselves in the sun to gain a potent weapon via a Devotion.</a> Give it a look, when you have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T07:14:58-08:00","id":824929,"title":"","content":"It is very interesting, indeed. Not quite the theme of this Coil, but ideas to digest.<br /> <br /> For now, though, I just thought of the vampire being able to use Damage from sunlight as a source of bonuses. Maybe this: every time the Dragon suffer damage from sunlight, it adds dice to a pile of Coil Bonus Dice. 1 die for 1 non-lethal, 2 dice for 1 lethal, 3 dice for 1 Aggravated. Those dice endure by day, but by night they only linger if the damage isn't healed.<br /> <br /> Dice from this pile can be used to augment rolls against the Beast. Frenzy, R\u00f6tschreck, or any other roll described as the vampire struggling with the urges of the Beast, or even to control it, can be increased with those dice. Yes, you can use this power even to Ride the Wave. Indeed, it would be interesting to use such bonuses with the Coil of the Wyrm. But it can also be used with the Coil of the Ascendant.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the dice can be used to augment Humanity for the purposes of its benefits. This consumes 2 dice per +1. The bonus endures for all the day, but only one scene by night. Once the dice are used, the damage can be healed without further problems, but the burned flesh lingers as for Fortitude, except it can only be healed by night.<br /> <br /> The vampire with this Coil don't need ever to roll for R\u00f6tschreck when suffering sunlight damage or facing the sun in any other way. But there are no other direct benefits without help of other Coil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T07:22:43-08:00","id":824931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813864-mystery-of-humanities?p=824929#post824929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is very interesting, indeed. Not quite the theme of this Coil, but ideas to digest.<br /> <br /> For now, though, I just thought of the vampire being able to use Damage from sunlight as a source of bonuses. Maybe this: every time the Dragon suffer damage from sunlight, it adds dice to a pile of Coil Bonus Dice. 1 die for 1 non-lethal, 2 dice for 1 lethal, 3 dice for 1 Aggravated. Those dice endure by day, but by night they only linger if the damage isn't healed.<br /> <br /> Dice from this pile can be used to augment rolls against the Beast. Frenzy, R\u00f6tschreck, or any other roll described as the vampire struggling with the urges of the Beast, or even to control it, can be increased with those dice. Yes, you can use this power even to Ride the Wave. Indeed, it would be interesting to use such bonuses with the Coil of the Wyrm. But it can also be used with the Coil of the Ascendant.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the dice can be used to augment Humanity for the purposes of its benefits. This consumes 2 dice per +1. The bonus endures for all the day, but only one scene by night. Once the dice are used, the damage can be healed without further problems, but the burned flesh lingers as for Fortitude, except it can only be healed by night.<br /> <br /> The vampire with this Coil don't need ever to roll for R\u00f6tschreck when suffering sunlight damage or facing the sun in any other way. But there are no other direct benefits without help of other Coil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Definitely a promising idea. Looking forward to seeing this better polished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T03:54:49-08:00","id":827390,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HrR6VU-PdpQ543RIorAh1GVERBuwg3WeMhQEfqG7mLI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Monteparnas' Coil of Humanity, because I got carried by the idea. In the same way, I would like for people to see and say what they think. It isn't done yet, I didn't even touched level 4 until now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:44:19-08:00","id":827714,"title":"","content":"Monteparnas I have enjoyed looking at your spin on the Mystery and while I have not had time to very closely examine your work I am excited to do so when I get the time to return to working on this pet project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T22:17:35-07:00","id":895299,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mystery of the Humanities</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Often the Mystery of Humanity is spurned as a Heretical teaching created in effort to escape Vamprism and return to Humanity, instead of Transcending Vamprisim. The teaching of the Coils of Humanities is banned in a great many Ordo Dracul Chapter Houses across the World, and even where it's teachings are not banned out right, the Mystery of Humanities and it's Coils are very rarely studied or practiced. In truth the Ordo of Dracul has found no means of actually measuring the progress of any student of the Mystery of Humanities and so never is any claimed progress in the Mystery allowed to be part of any Dragon's Covenant Rank, Status, or Title.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> The Mystery of Humanity was not created in effort to escape Vampirism and revert back to being Human.The truth of the Mystery though is that it was created to aid the Man in his eternal struggle against the Beast. The creator of the Mystery of Humanity believed that the greatest bane of the Vampric condition was the slow but inevitable erosion of self.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The lessons learned through exploring the Mystery of Humanity are lessons of the Humanities such as Art, Philosophy, Morality, Ethics, and Logic. The Humanities though are not studied though in effort to force Morality upon the Vampire, or in Effort to once more to become Human. They are studied to better draw the divide the between the Vampire's Mind and the Beast. Dragons who have mastered the Mystery of Humanity and it's Coils have learned to separate their own choices from the Beast's desires and demands, regardless of the morality of the choices they choose to make.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Coils of the Humanities</u></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sisyphean Fortitude\u2022</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is an ever present current of want, eroding away what Humanity remains until nothing remains but want. Those who have mastered this coil have learned to better endure the storm that is the every present threat of the Beast upon their Sanity. Whenever the Dragon rolls for Detachment add their Coils of Humanities Rank to their Detachment Dice Pool to maintain Humanity. In addition to this an Exceptional Success can be achieved with 3 Successes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Koinonein \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To Divide and Conquer is a time tested and proven tactic, and the Beast knows it well. One of the more subtle and ruthless attacks upon the Mind of the Man is the Beast's efforts to isolate the Man from others. By making the Man feel removed from Humanity, he is removed from the herd and easier prey for the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil have learned how to keep thier place in the Herd dispite the Beast's best efforts. Add the Dragon's ranks in the Coils of Humanities in regards to interacting with Humanity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Man beneath Morpheus \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is never truly at rest. Even within the deep hibernation of Torpor, or the slumber of Day Sleep the Beast is Hungry for more, it's mind races with the revelry of past and future hunts, always denying the mind of Man the Rest it needs to fully recover. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanity are no longer the victims of the beast's unsated hungers when they close their eyes. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil of Humanities may regain 1 point of Willpower from Day Sleep the same as Mortals regain Willpower from a Night's Rest.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prometheus in the Cave of Hypnos\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The forced Hibernation of Torpor is another of the Beasts threats to the Mind of Man. Through removing the Man from Humanity for vast cycles of time it forces the Man to see himself as an entity separate from the present, separate from the People of Today, always a creature of the past and of the future. In making the Man unfocused upon the present and uncaring for those who live within it, the Beast makes it easier for the Man to give in to the ever present Temptations of the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered this Coil have learned to steel themselves against the Beast's Call to Hibernate as an Animal. Dragons add their ranks in the Coil of Humanities to their Humanity for purposes of determining the length of their Torpor, and rolls to resist Day Sleep, and or Awaking from Day Sleep.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Human under Helios \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast is a Nocturnal Predator, Man is not. The Light of Day does not Burn Man, it Burns the Beast. Dragons who have Mastered the Fifth and Final Coil of Humanities stand dominate over the Beast, while it cowers in the shadow of Man. Because the Dragon's Beast cowers within the shadow of Man, the Dragon is afforded some protection from the light of day. Add the Dragon's ranks in the Coil of Humanities to their Humanity to determine the damage they take from Sun light.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Scales of Humanity</u></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Lessons of Humility</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite Coils:</b> Koinonein</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Procedure:</b> Over the course of an hour the Dragon is able to remind his subject of the frailty of Mortal Men and the many hardships they endure through out their existence. This conditioning can when successful aid even the most jaded kindred in remembering how to empathize with others and understand their prey in a way they had forgotten. For a short time the subject may once more remember what it meant to be a mere mortal and once more move among them seeing them for more then mere meals.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Dragon needs to roll Presence + Expression.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Roll Results</u></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Dragon has rambled on and on about the weaknesses of humanity and has failed to inspire sympathy for mortals, and instead stirred the Beast within himself and his audience. Both the Dragon and his Subject gain the Wanton Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Failure: </b>The Dragon's meaningless words fall upon deaf and uncaring ears.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Success: </b>The Dragon's words once more, if only for a Night, remind the Subject of the plight of Man Kind. The Subject may add the Dragon's Successes to his Humanity for one Night in regards to how Humanity effects interaction with Mortals.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> Same as a Success, and the Jaded Condition if possessed is resolved.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Startling The Slumbering</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite Coil:</b> Prometheus in the Cave of Hypnos</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Procedure:</b> The Dragon must spend their Day Sleep along side the Torpored Subject, and upon waking immediately feed a minimal of one point of Vitae to the subject. For every Vitae feed to the subject in this manner a die is rolled, and Successes are added to the Subject's Humanity Score for purposes of determining the length of their Torpor. This procedure can be repeated day after day and night after night with all the successes rolled working towards raising the Subjects Humanity for the purpose of awakening from Torpor.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T22:36:14-07:00","id":895310,"title":"","content":"Hmm. So far, this latest write-up on the Mystery of Humanities looks really good.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}